[b]Welcome to the Forum![/b]

This is a sample BBCode post demonstrating common forum markup features.
BBCode is widely used in phpBB, vBulletin, and other forum software.

[b]Text Formatting[/b]

[b]Bold text[/b] makes things stand out.
[i]Italic text[/i] adds emphasis.
[u]Underlined text[/u] for important terms.
[s]Strikethrough text[/s] for corrections.
[b][i]Bold and italic combined[/i][/b] for extra emphasis.

[color=red]Red text[/color] and [color=#0066cc]blue text[/color] add color.
[size=18]Large text[/size] and [size=10]small text[/size] control font size.

[b]Links[/b]

[url=https://www.phpbb.com]Visit phpBB[/url]
[url=https://stackoverflow.com]Stack Overflow[/url]
Plain URL: [url]https://example.com[/url]

[b]Images[/b]

[img]https://example.com/avatar.png[/img]

Image with dimensions:
[img width=200 height=150]https://example.com/screenshot.png[/img]

[b]Quotes[/b]

[quote=Alice]
This is what Alice said in the previous post. It can span multiple lines
and includes all her formatting.
[/quote]

[quote=Bob post_id=12345]
Bob replied to the original question with this response.
[/quote]

[quote]
Anonymous quote without attribution.
[/quote]

[b]Code[/b]

Inline code: [code]print("Hello, World!")[/code]

Code block:
[code]def fibonacci(n):
    if n <= 1:
        return n
    return fibonacci(n-1) + fibonacci(n-2)

print(fibonacci(10))  # Output: 55[/code]

Syntax-highlighted code:
[code=python]class Stack:
    def __init__(self):
        self.items = []

    def push(self, item):
        self.items.append(item)

    def pop(self):
        return self.items.pop()
[/code]

